fear, to walk in all His ways, to love Him, to serve, to keep — 6:13's fear and serve, 8:6's walk and fear, 6:5's love: three cells' verbs in one question"}; and_you_shall_love_five = [('Deut 6:5', 'ואהבת'), ('Deut 10:19', 'ואהבתם'), ('Deut 11:1', 'ואהבת'), ('Lev 19:18', 'ואהבת'), ('Lev 19:34', 'ואהבת')]; you_were_strangers_four = ['Deut 10:19', 'Exod 22:20', 'Exod 23:9', 'Lev 19:34']; ten_twenty_against_six_thirteen = {'6_13': ['את', 'יהוה', 'אלהיך', 'תירא', 'ואתו', 'תעבד', 'ובשמו', 'תשבע'], '10_20': ['את', 'יהוה', 'אלהיך', 'תירא', 'אתו', 'תעבד', 'ובו', 'תדבק', 'ובשמו', 'תשבע'], 'the_diff': [('replace', ['אתו'], ['ואתו']), ('delete', ['ובו', 'תדבק'], [])], 'the_shared': 7}; the_heaven_of_heavens_six = {'with_the_vav': ['1Kgs 8:27', '2Chr 2:5', '2Chr 6:18', 'Deut 10:14'], 'without': ['Neh 9:6', 'Ps 148:4']}; the_parsers_first = {'the_plural': [('כראשנים', 1), ('הראשנים', 2), ('כראשנים', 3), ('הראשנים', 10)], 'the_singular': [('הראשון', 4)], 'the_ordinals': {4: [1]}, 'the_numbers': {1: [2], 3: [2, 2], 4: [10], 10: [40, 40], 22: [70]}}; no_memra = NO MEMRA (the Word) IN THE CHAPTER — Onkelos renders the LORD's speech and acts without the Word at every verse (chapter 9's three seats at 9:3, 9:8, 9:20 by contrast); the gifts supplied at 10:9, 'to His fear you shall draw near' at 10:20 (the cleaving made drawing near), 'the foolishness of your heart' at 10:16 (the foreskin made foolishness), 'the God of judges and the Lord of kings' at 10:17; the_seventys_three_forms = {'genesis_46_27': "'all the persons of the house of Jacob that came into Egypt were seventy' — the count's seat (the parser [2, 70]: Joseph's two sons and the seventy)", 'exodus_1_5': "'and all the persons that came out of the loins of Jacob were seventy persons' — the restatement (the parser [70]; JS.seventy('exodus_seventy') = 70)", 'deut_10_22': "'with SEVENTY PERSONS your fathers went down to Egypt' — the retelling's (the parser [70]; 'with seventy persons' the one seat)", 'jochebed': 'jochebed_born_between_the_walls', 'diverge': 'DIVERGE_leah_33_vs_32_living', 'the_register': "the count seat Deut 10:22 kept NONE with the compile's why — the cell by CALL, no row on the population table (Exodus 1:5's form: a restated total seeds nothing)"}; kings_reads_the_ark = {'1_kings_8_9': "'there was nothing in the ark except the two tablets of stone which Moses put there at Horeb' — Solomon's dedication reading the ark's contents from THIS telling (four tokens shared with 10:5; the parser [2] at 8:9); R. Yehuda's double restriction 'nothing … except' the fragments' third derivation (E4)", 'and_there_they_are': ['1Chr 12:40', '1Kgs 8:8', '2Sam 2:18', '2Sam 4:3', 'Deut 10:5', 'Josh 4:9', 'Ruth 1:2']}; the_charge_to_joshua = {'31_7': "Moses to Joshua — 'for you shall go with this people into the land which the LORD swore to their fathers to give them' (seven tokens shared with 10:11)", 'joshua_1_6': "God to Joshua — 'you shall cause this people to inherit the land which I swore to their fathers to give them' (seven tokens shared)", 'the_shared': ['את', 'הארץ', 'אשר', 'נשבעתי']}; ark_of_the_covenant_vs_testimony = {'deuteronomy': ['Deut 10:8', 'Deut 31:25', 'Deut 31:26', 'Deut 31:9'], 'joshua': ['Josh 3:3', 'Josh 4:18', 'Josh 4:7', 'Josh 8:33'], 'exodus': ['Exod 26:34', 'Exod 30:26', 'Exod 40:5', 'Exod 26:33', 'Exod 40:21', 'Exod 40:3', 'Josh 4:16'], 'the_count': 33}; the_grammar_guard = {'the_row': "Shabbat 108a:7 — the verbal analogy (I2) 'his foreskin' (Leviticus 12:3) / 'its foreskin' (19:23): circumcision in THAT place; the analogy takes the COMPLETE form orlato / orlato and REFUSES the construct — 'the foreskin of your heart' (10:16), 'the foreskins of your heart' (Jeremiah 4:4), 'the foreskin of the ear' (6:10)", 'the_forms': {'10_16': ['עָרְלַת'], 'lev_12_3_and_19_23': [('Lev 12:3', 'ערלתו'), ('Lev 19:23', 'ערלתו')]}, 'the_finding': "THE HEART'S FORESKIN IS NOT THE CIRCUMCISION LAW'S OBJECT — circumcision_due's twenty-four entries all the flesh's (DB7); heart_circumcision_commanded a new name"}; the_inclinations_name = {'the_row': "Sukkah 52a:7 — THE EVIL INCLINATION HAS SEVEN NAMES: the Holy One called it EVIL (Genesis 8:21), MOSES called it FORESKIN ('and you shall circumcise the foreskin of your heart' — 10:16), David UNCLEAN (Psalm 51:12), Solomon ENEMY (Proverbs 25:21), Isaiah STUMBLING BLOCK (57:14), Ezekiel STONE (36:26), Joel THE HIDDEN ONE (2:20)", 'the_value': "heart_circumcision_commanded's value — the evil inclination (Moses' name for it, from this verse)", 'the_kin': ['Deut 10:16', 'Jer 4:4', 'Lev 26:41', 'Ezek 44:7', 'Jer 9:25']}; the_burial_among_the_attributes = {'the_row': "Sotah 14a:3-4 — 'after the LORD your God you shall walk' (13:5): walk after His attributes — He clothed the naked (Genesis 3:21), visited the sick (18:1), comforted mourners (25:11), BURIED THE DEAD ('and He buried him in the valley', 34:6); 14a:6 — the Torah begins with kindness and ends with kindness", 'the_chapter': "10:6's PASSIVE burial ('and he was buried there' — by no named hand) beside 34:6's (by God's hand): the burial's two forms at the two deaths of the brothers", 'the_seat': ['Deut 10:6']}; the_positive_form = {'the_rows': "Temurah 4a:2 — 'you shall fear the LORD your God' A WARNING STATED AS A POSITIVE COMMAND (the blasphemer's warning from it — Sanhedrin 56a:11); Temurah 3b:17-18 — Rav Giddel: 'and by His name you shall swear' a positive command, a truthful oath permitted", 'the_four': [('תירא', 'HVqi2ms'), ('תעבד', 'HVqi2ms'), ('תדבק', 'HVqi2ms'), ('תשבע', 'HVNi2ms')], 'the_finding': "10:20's four clauses positive (the imperfects without 'not') — STATUS not BLOCK: cleaving_commanded a status, no lashes; the chapter's one BLOCK 10:16's neck"}; the_converts_intake = {'the_rows': "Yevamot 47a:13-47b:15 — the intake's procedure: 'what did you see that you come? do you not know that Israel today are afflicted …?' — 'I know and I am unworthy' accepted at once; informed of some minor and some major commandments, gleanings, the forgotten sheaf, the corner, the poor tithe, the punishments and the rewards; circumcised and immersed an Israelite in all respects (47b:15); the evidence dispute (47a:1, 47a:6); the convert in court from 1:16 (47a:7); the private convert not believed (47a:8-12); the slave and the captive (47b:16-19)", 'the_finding': "'for you were strangers' (10:19) told to the convert at his intake — the stranger line's exam; the private convert exempt from the standing"}; the_editors_variant = {'the_ink': "Numbers 33:38 — 'in the fortieth year … in the FIFTH month, on the first of the month': the ordinal reader [40, 5], the number reader [1] — the first of Av; the tape's marker at Num 20:28 (40, 5, 1) = (40, 5, 1)", 'the_variant': "the export's Seder Olam Rabbah 10:2 carries 'the first of Tammuz' in one arm of the chapter's text — THE EDITOR'S VARIANT, a DATA note; the ink's fifth month the tape's; Seder Olam 9:2 and the shelf's rows Aaron in Av", 'the_burial': "the burial line dated at the same day — M['burial_told'] = M['aaron_death']"}; the_face_thrice_reconciled = {'the_contradiction': "'who lifts no face' (10:17) against 'the LORD lift up His face to you' (Numbers 6:26)", 'sifrei_42_2': "when Israel do His will He lifts His face, when not He lifts no face — the Naso cell's DATA face_lifted = when_they_do_his_will", 'berakhot_20b_15': "the ministering angels' question — shall I not lift My face to Israel, who go beyond the letter: I wrote 'you shall eat and be satisfied and bless' (8:10) and they bless on an olive's bulk", 'niddah_70b_5': "the sages of Alexandria's form — before the sentence is passed / after", 'rosh_hashanah_17b_17': "Beloria the convert's question — between man and God the face is lifted, between man and man not (R. Yosei the priest)", 'the_seats': (['Deut 10:17', 'Deut 28:50'], ['Num 6:26'])}; the_six_judges = {'shmuel': "a man gave him his hand crossing on a plank — 'I am disqualified from judging you' (Ketubot 105b:8)", 'ameimar': 'a feather removed from his head (105b:9)', 'mar_ukva': 'spittle covered (105b:10)', 'r_yishmael_bar_r_yosei': "his sharecropper's basket brought a day early — disqualified himself; as the case was argued he wished the man would win: 'cursed be those who take bribes' (105b:11-12)", 'r_yishmael_bar_elisha': 'the first shearing brought by a man with a case (105b:13-14)', 'rav_anan': 'a fish brought by a man with a case (105b:15)', 'the_rule': "the bribe of WORDS disqualifies — shochad = she-hu chad (105b:5, E30); a bribe even to judge truly (105a:10); the bribe blinds the wise a fortiori the foolish (105a:16, I1); Karna's fee for evident loss permitted (105a:17-19); a salary voids (Kiddushin 58b)"}; the_uncited_verses = [3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 9, 11, 13, 15, 19, 21, 22]; the_credits = {'the_seventh_b': "Menachot 99a-b whole from 7b's docket (the fragments in the ark; the breaking approved); Menachot 43b from chapter 6's (the hundred blessings); Bava Batra 14a-b in part, Sotah 14a, Megillah 25a, Berakhot 8b two rows from earlier dockets", 'the_count': "257 of 532 credited by address at the scan — the writer's computed count"} (the other settings recorded in DATA)

